Speech2Anywhere -- Voice-to-Text Tool
Personal-Use License
Version 0.1, 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 Mike Pollow / Digitalroots

This software was developed for personal use. By installing or using
the software, you agree to the following terms:

1. Personal use
   The software may be used by you and people in your immediate circle.
   Distribution to third parties or commercial exploitation requires
   the author's written consent.

2. No warranty
   The software is provided "as is", without express or implied warranty.
   The author is not liable for any damage arising from use.

3. Local data processing
   Speech2Anywhere processes all voice and text data exclusively on your local
   machine. Voice and text data are not transmitted to the author's or
   third-party servers. Speech2Anywhere connects to the internet only for the update
   check (GitHub Releases API) at start, at regular intervals (every six
   hours by default) and on request, for downloading an update you have
   confirmed, and for loading speech recognition and language models from
   Hugging Face and the Ollama registry; the automatic update checks can be
   switched off in config.yaml (updates.check_on_start). The bundled
   Ollama app checks for its own updates.

4. Third-party software
   The installation includes components under their own licenses
   (Python, faster-whisper, Ollama, Gemma, PyQt6, pystray, and others).
   Their license terms continue to apply unchanged.

Contact: Mike Pollow
GitHub:  https://github.com/MikeGT4/speech2anywhere

